title: PostRJMemory
---
<<declare $CousinName = "Damir">>

<<changeSprite 1 0>>
<<changeSprite 2 0>>
<<twoChar>>

<<darken 2>>
<<lighten 1>>
{$lover2Name}: And there really isn't much else for us to say…
<<darken 1>>

{$protagName}: So you got out, but what happened to {$CousinName}?

<<lighten 2>>   // Change Jovan's Expression: Frown
{$lover1Name} opens and closes his mouth as if to speak.
<<darken 2>>

<<lighten 1>>   // Change Ruzica's Expression: Soft
{$lover2Name}:  We can never repay {$CousinName} for what he did for us.
<<darken 1>>

<<lighten 2>>
{$lover1Name}: He died-
<<darken 2>>

<<lighten 1>>
{$lover2Name}: {$lover1Name}...
<<darken 1>>

<<lighten 2>>
{$lover1Name}: They burned his house and he died.
<<darken 2>>

<<lighten 1>>   // Change Ruzica's Expression: Angry
{$lover2Name} glares at {$protagName}.
<<darken 1>>

<<lighten 2>>   // Change Jovan's Expression: Grieving
{$lover1Name} closes his eyes.
{$lover1Name}: {$CousinName} is why we're here. He deserved to be remembered.
<<darken 2>>

<<lighten 1>>   // Change Ruzica's Expression: Soft
{$lover2Name}'s expression softens.
{$lover2Name}: We stopped by a bakery to buy his favorite cake.
<<darken 1>>

<<lighten 2>>   // Change Jovan's Expression: Smile
{$lover1Name} smiles.
{$lover1Name}: He loved chocolate cake. It drove our family crazy. He never shared either.
<<darken 2>>

<<lighten 1>>   // Change Ruzica's Expression: Smile
{$lover2Name} smiles too.
{$lover2Name}: {$CousinName} had a good taste in dessert.
<<darken 1>>

{$lover1Name} and {$lover2Name} sit in silence for a while.
<<darken 2>>
<<darken 1>>
{$protagName}: Well, thank you for sharing your story.

<<lighten 2>>
{$lover1Name}: Our pleasure.
<<darken 2>>

<<lighten 1>>
{$lover2Name}: While we're here, we should take a look at the other exhibits.
<<darken 1>>

<<lighten 2>>
{$lover1Name}: That sounds like a wonderful idea.
<<darken 2>>

<<lighten 1>>
{$lover2Name}: Bye, {$protagName}! I hope we were able to help with the tree.
<<darken 1>>
<<zeroChar>>
{$lover1Name} and {$lover2Name} walk away, hand-in-hand.
===

title: PostRJPetarStart
---
<<oneChar>>
<<changeSprite 1 4>>
<<lighten 1>>
{$directorName}: How did the interview go? You didn't upset them, did you?
-> Could've been better. Don't think I upset them, though.
    {$protagName}: Could've been better. Don't think I upset them, though.
-> I think it went pretty well.
    {$protagName}: I think it went pretty well.
-> Excellent!
    {$protagName}: Excellent!
{$directorName}: We'll see about that.
<<zeroChar>>
===

title: PostMemRJStart
---
<<twoChar>>
<<changeSprite 1 0>>
<<changeSprite 2 0>>
<<changeStat 0 2>>

<<darken 1>>
<<lighten 2>>
{$lover1Name}: Oh, hello again.
<<darken 2>>

{$protagName}: I'm happy to see that you're exploring the museum.

<<lighten 2>>
{$lover1Name}: It's a lovely museum!
<<darken 2>>

{$protagName}: Is there anything in particular you like?

<<lighten 2>>
{$lover1Name}: I like the inclusion of children's toys. Too often, people forget about the children in those situations.
<<darken 2>>

<<lighten 1>>
{$lover2Name}: I agree. It's depressing, but necessary.
<<darken 1>>

{$protagName}: It sounds like this is important to you both.
<<jump PostMemRJChildren>>
===

title: PostMemRJChildren
---
<<lighten 2>>
{$lover1Name}: I'm a teacher. I had just started my career when the war started, and I had to leave those students behind when we left.
<<darken 2>>
-> I'm sure they were in good hands.
    {$protagName}: I'm sure they were in good hands.
    <<changeStat 0 1>>
    <<lighten 1>>
    {$lover2Name}: In times of war, there's no guarantee.
    <<darken 1>>
    <<lighten 2>>
    {$lover1Name}: Still, I like to hope.
    <<darken 2>>
    -> Hope is a good thing to have.
        {$protagName}: Hope is a good thing to have.
        <<lighten 2>>
        {$lover1Name}: It's what keeps us going.
        <<darken 2>>
        <<jump PostMemRJEnd>>
    -> Have you checked in on them?
        <<changeStat 0 2>>
        {$protagName}: Have you checked in on them?
        <<lighten 2>>
        {$lover1Name}: I've tried, but-
        <<darken 2>>
        <<lighten 1>>
        {$lover2Name}: I think it's best if we stop here.
        <<darken 1>>
        <<jump PostMemRJEnd>>
-> That must have been difficult on top of everything.
    {$protagName}: That must have been difficult on top of everything.
    <<lighten 2>>
    {$lover1Name}: It really was.
    <<darken 2>>
    <<lighten 1>>
    {$lover2Name}: Hopefully, we never have to go through that again.
    <<darken 1>>
    {$protagName}: As long as you have each other.
    <<lighten 1>>
    {$lover2Name} smiles.
    {$lover2Name}: I suppose so.
    <<darken 1>>
    <<jump PostMemRJEnd>>
===

title: PostMemRJEnd
---
<<lighten 2>>
{$lover1Name}: Well, it was nice talking to you again!
<<darken 2>>

{$protagName}: You too.

<<zeroChar>>
{$lover1Name} and {$lover2Name} leave.
===